WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.760
We ask a lot of questions
about our diet.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.080
What’s the right way to
treat a chronic illness?

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.720
Fight off a virus,
lose weight?

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.640
The problem is, we get
a lot of different answers.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.880
Well, I’m here to help.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.200
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:27.640
A century ago, the age of first
menstruation averaged as late as nearly 17.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.760
So, why is sexual maturity
coming so much earlier now?

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.520
Here’s our first story.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.320
Healthy Seventh-day Adventist
vegetarians

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.880
may be longest living,
but might that come at a cost?

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.320
A semen analysis

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.760
at a fertility clinic
in Loma Linda, California,

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:47.240
home to a large population
of Adventists,

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.080
raised questions
about their sperm quality.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.080
Though still within
the normal range,

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.320
vegetarians had about
a 25 percent lower sperm count.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:59.520
The few vegans tested also had
a lower sperm concentration,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.200
but they made up for that

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.240
with their 30 percent
greater ejaculate volume.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.320
The vegans did have

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.680
significantly fewer
activated sperm, though,

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:11.080
which is a sign
of decreased fertility.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.520
The researchers suggested
soy consumption

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.200
as a possible mechanism,

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.360
as Adventist vegetarians
in California

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.400
average
about a half serving a day

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.680
of plant-based meats,
many of which contain soy.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.400
Soy phytoestrogens have been
put to the test, though,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.800
and months of consuming

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:31.160
up to the equivalent of nearly
20 servings of soy a day

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.360
did not result
in any adverse effects

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.120
on sperm parameters.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.560
There were only five vegans
in the study,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.640
so the sperm quality findings
could just be a fluke,

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.640
but if verified,
this could reflect

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:48.480
an evolutionary trade-off
between fertility and lifespan

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.360
first proposed
nearly a century ago.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.360
Using a finely tuned laser,

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:57.080
it's possible to selectively
destroy individual cells

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.840
as the tiny roundworm
C. elegans develops,

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.160
and terminating the cells

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.520
that give rise
to sperm and eggs

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.920
significantly extends lifespan.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.680
The same phenomenon can be
demonstrated in fruit flies,

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.600
potentially shifting
the body's priorities

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:16.040
from reproduction to survival.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.640
The fertility
versus longevity trade-off

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:19.720
may be one of the reasons why

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.320
spaying and neutering
our pets

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.280
can extend their lives.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.040
Based on a study
of millions of dogs and cats,

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.640
sterilized dogs
live about 20 percent longer

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.280
than "intact" dogs,

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.720
and spayed cats
live about 40 percent longer,

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:40.040
and neutered cats
a remarkable 60 percent longer.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.760
What about men
who have been castrated?

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.640
Eunuchs seem to live
25 percent longer

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.760
than non-castrated men.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.920
Up until the 1950s
in the United States,

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.320
the so-called "feebleminded"
were involuntary sterilized

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.920
by the state
in a eugenics program

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.040
upheld by none other than
Oliver Wendell Holmes,

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:03.080
who wrote for the majority
on the Supreme Court:

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:07.280
"[S]ociety can prevent those
who are manifestly unfit

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:09.960
from continuing their kind.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.560
The principle that sustains
compulsory vaccination

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.680
is broad enough to cover
cutting the Fallopian tubes."

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.800
The heinous practice
of compulsory sterilization

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.800
did allow for
a natural experiment, though,

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.600
and one mental institution
found that castrated men

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:31.200
lived about 14 years longer
than intact men

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.080
in the same hospital.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.520
A genealogy database
of nearly 200,000 men and women

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.240
across three centuries
in 16 countries

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.120
found that those
who had fewer children

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.240
seemed to live longer.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.120
Centenarians, for example,
were found

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.960
to have fewer children
at later ages.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:50.400
This is not to suggest
that having fewer children

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.840
will make you live longer,

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.280
but rather
that constitutional factors

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:58.080
that enhance human lifespan
may come at the expense

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.440
of reduced
reproductive potential,

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:03.560
another example of the
antagonistic pleiotropy theory

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.320
I talked about before.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.760
For example, selection
for lifespan extension

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.280
in model organisms can lead
to longer lived animals

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.800
but with reduced
reproductive capacity.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.680
It makes intuitive sense

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:20.360
when you consider the context
of food scarcity.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.800
In lean times, it makes sense
to put off reproduction

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.880
until the return
of more favorable conditions

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:28.320
to ensure long-term survival.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:31.240
In the infamous
Minnesota Starvation Study

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:34.200
that used conscientious
objectors as guinea pigs

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.680
during World War II,

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:39.400
the study subjects
rapidly lost their libidos

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.840
after their calorie intake
was cut in half.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.200
As one of them put it,

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:49.080
"I have no more sexual feeling
than a sick oyster."

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.280
The same calorie restriction

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:51.880
that extends
the lives of animals

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:55.440
can also cause a reduction
in the number of progeny.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.120
If you read my book
How Not to Age,

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.160
you'll be familiar

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:02.000
with the nutrient-sensing
aging pathways--

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.320
IGF-1, mTOR, AMPK--

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.080
that create kind of a seesaw

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.760
between tissue acceleration
and reproduction on one side

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:15.200
and tissue preservation
and rejuvenation on the other.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.840
Thankfully, we can shift
the weight

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:20.880
to a more optimal balance
with diet.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.960
The later girls
start their periods,

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.680
the longer they tend to live.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.400
Each year later is associated
with significantly lower risk

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:30.920
of dying from heart disease
and stroke, plateauing out

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:32.600
with the lowest
overall mortality

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:36.680
among those who don't start
menstruating until age 15.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:39.040
Isn't 15 a little late?

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.160
It didn't used to be.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:42.960
A century ago,
the age of first menstruation

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.040
averaged as late as nearly 17.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:48.160
Similarly, the age
of breast development

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.680
has dropped an average of
about three months per decade

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:53.080
over the last half century
around the world,

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.960
down to 9 or 10 years old
in the United States,

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.760
necessitating a change
in textbook definitions

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:03.000
of quote-unquote
"premature" puberty.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.200
Earlier breast development
(before age 10 versus 12 or 13)

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.920
is associated
with as much as 23 percent

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.320
greater breast cancer risk
later in life,

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:14.960
and each year later
a girl starts to menstruate

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:17.480
is linked
to significantly lower risk

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:20.280
of cancers of the uterus,
liver, skin,

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.840
bladder, colon, lung,
and breast.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.080
Thankfully, the age of puberty
is something

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:27.920
over which we have
a degree of control.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.840
Higher levels of IGF-1
are associated

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:33.320
with earlier sexual maturity,

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:36.160
so it's no surprise that girls
eating more animal protein

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.840
experience puberty
significantly earlier,

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:41.920
an effect not seen
with protein from plants.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.760
A meta-analysis of 16 studies
on diet and development

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:46.720
found that one's first period

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:49.720
appears to start earlier
by two months

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.680
for each additional
one gram per day

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.920
of animal protein intake
in childhood.

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:56.640
So, for example,
at seven years old,

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:59.840
girls consuming more than
12 servings of meat a week

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:02.800
had 75 percent greater odds
of menstruating

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.520
within the next five years
or so

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:05.760
compared to girls at that age

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:08.160
eating less than
four servings a week,

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.280
and this relationship was seen
for both red meat

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.240
and poultry consumption.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.760
IGF-1 and other aging pathways

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:17.200
may not fully explain
these findings, however,

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.720
as persistent pollutants
that build up in meat, like DDT,

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:24.667
have also been linked
to precocious puberty.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:25.800
In our last story,

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.000
we look at how the early
onset of puberty in girls

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:34.360
may be due to endocrine-disrupting
chemical pollutants in the meat supply.

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:38.120
“Early onset of puberty is
considered a…risk factor…

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:43.440
[for] a number of diseases in adulthood,
including hormone-related cancers,

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:48.920
[a shorter lifespan], metabolic
syndrome, and cardiovascular disease.”

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:51.880
The conventional thinking
has been that the reason the

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:54.280
age of puberty has been
getting earlier and earlier

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:57.200
is because our children have been
getting fatter and fatter.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:01.840
Well, our kids have been getting heavier,
especially in the United States—

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.400
we’re #1!

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:09.200
But, while the age of a girl’s first period
has been dropping in the U.S. and Asia,

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.480
in Europe—despite their kids
getting heavier, too—

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:15.920
there hasn’t been a steady
decline in puberty onset.

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:19.280
So, maybe it’s less about
how much kids are eating,

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:21.800
and more about
what they’re eating.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:25.600
The most consistent link between
diet and premature puberty

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:28.480
has been animal protein consumption.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:32.400
For example, every gram of
daily animal protein intake—

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.520
that’s the weight of a paperclip—

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:38.160
has been associated with about
a 17% increase in the risk

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:42.120
of girls starting their periods
earlier than age 12.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:45.360
Why this link between animal protein
and premature puberty?

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:50.360
Well, we know meat increases the
levels of the growth hormone IGF-1,

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:53.800
and that alone is associated
with early-onset puberty.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:57.840
But, maybe animal protein is just a
proxy for the endocrine-disrupting

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:01.320
chemicals that build up the
food chain in animal products.

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:03.000
Recent reports found

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.320
“significant associations
between exposure to

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:08.960
environmental pollutants
and sexual maturation.”

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:10.600
This was done over in Europe.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.480
In the U.S.,
a similar relationship was found

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:15.840
with the flame-retardant chemicals,
for example,

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:23.160
which are found mostly in poultry
and fish, unless you’re eating cat food.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.960
“Over the last three decades,
human exposure

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.720
[to these levels of industrial pollutants]

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.520
in the U.S. have increased
from virtually nonexistent to

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:34.360
[almost everyone carrying
them around now].”

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:36.560
They appear to have
multiple adverse effects,

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:38.640
but of all the potential toxicities,

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:42.280
endocrine disruption
(meaning hormonal disruption)

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:45.600
may be the main
concern in children.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:50.240
Girls with the most circulating in their
bloodstream appeared up to ten times

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:52.880
more likely to start
their periods early.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:55.720
But, since these chemicals are found
most concentrated in fish and chicken,

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:58.080
maybe the level of these
chemicals in their bloodstream

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.960
is just kind of a proxy
for their meat consumption.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:04.040
Whatever the reason,
animal protein intake

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.760
is associated with
early-onset puberty,

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.640
whereas plant protein
has the opposite effect.

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:13.720
Children with higher levels of
vegetable proteins starting puberty

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:17.880
seven months later than average,
and children eating more animal protein

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:21.320
may start puberty seven months
earlier than average.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:22.920
Soy seems most protective.

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:26.200
“[G]irls with the highest levels
of dietary isoflavone intake

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.320
[the phytonutrients in soy foods]

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:30.440
may experience their onset
of breast development…

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:36.840
approximately 7 or 8 months later than
girls with the lowest levels of intake.”

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:39.880
What effect might these shifts
have on disease rates?

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:47.280
Well, delays in the timing of puberty
in response to beneficial dietary habits

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:52.040
(higher intakes of vegetable protein and
soy, and lower intakes of animal protein)

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:55.120
“may be of substantial
public health relevance.”

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:58.720
A later age of starting one’s period
is related to a reduced risk

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.200
of breast cancer,

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:04.120
and a later first period is associated
with lower total mortality

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.600
(meaning a longer lifespan).”

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:10.800
Hence, “a delay in the timing of puberty
by approximately 7-8 months,” which is

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:15.720
“achievable with dietary modifications”
—either more plants or fewer animals—”

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:19.600
may translate into about a 6%
reduction in breast cancer risk,”

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:23.360
and up to a 3%
decrease in total mortality.

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:26.720
And, it’s not just a problem in girls;
boys eating more meat in childhood

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:30.640
appear to be more likely to grow up
with the kind of abdominal fat deposits

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:34.517
that increase risk
for heart disease.

